Istio Setup:
============

Install Istio in K8s cluster:
1. Download istio in your Ubuntu WSL    //#curl -L https://istio.io/downloadIstio | sh
2. Move into the downloaded folder     //#cd istio-*
3. Add istioctl to PATH                //#export PATH=$PWD/bin:$PATH
4. Verify                              //#istioctl version
5. Create Istio namespace              //#kubectl create namespace istio-system 
6. Install Istio                      //#istioctl install -y  
7. Validate                           //#kubectl get pods -n istio-system

Enable automatic sidecar injection:
1. Create a namespace                //#kubectl create namespace demo
2. Enable Istio inject              //#kubectl label namespace demo istio-injection=enabled
3. Verify                           //#kubectl get ns demo --show-labels
4. Deploy a test app                 //#kubectl create deployment nginx --image=nginx -n demo
5. Expose it                        //#kubectl expose deployment nginx --port=80 -n demo

Inject istio into all future namespaces using Kyverno cluster policy:
1. Install Kyverno
    #kubectl create namespace kyverno
    #kubectl apply -f https://github.com/kyverno/kyverno/releases/latest/download/install.yaml
2. Validate
    #kubectl get pods -n kyverno
    You should see
      kyverno-admission-controller     Running
      kyverno-background-controller    Running
      kyverno-cleanup-controller       Running
3. Verify CRD exists    #kubectl get crd | grep kyverno
4. Apply a policy that automatically labels new namespaces
---
apiVersion: kyverno.io/v1
kind: ClusterPolicy
metadata:
  name: auto-istio-injection
spec:
  rules:
  - name: add-istio-label
    match:
      any:
      - resources:
          kinds:
          - Namespace
    mutate:
      patchStrategicMerge:
        metadata:
          labels:
            istio-injection: enabled
---
5. Verify that policy      #kubectl get clusterpolicy
6. Validate                #kubectl create ns atom
